  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-10-31T02:40:28.972Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Related Issue: https://feedback.vrchat.com/sdk-bug-reports/p/on-linux-build-and-test-doesnt-produce-a-built-avatar\n\nI recently switched to Linux (using Fedora 43) and I can't build and test worlds.\n\nOn windows, I would test with multiple clients to make sure my networking stuff works correctly, and I'd really like to do this on linux as it's my main OS now, there's just no way to build and test on Linux right now, so i've been uploading a world each time to test, and I can't really test with multiple clients (which I really need).\n\nI know Linux isn't really supported as a platform at the moment, but more and more people are switching to it and it would be nice to have some more SDK support so we can have feature parity and develop VRC content just as well as people can on Windows.",
